From 56e057c72fbd3105632c0d87b36e9acf2631ee70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:29:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] drm/mediatek: Add MT6789 display pipeline support

Add MediaTek MT6789 display subsystem match data across mtk_drm_drv
and the DDP subdrivers (OVL, RDMA, COLOR, CCORR, AAL, GAMMA).

MT6789 OVL0 and RDMA0 require shadow-register bypass
(DISP_OVL_BYPASS_SHADOW in DISP_REG_OVL_EN and
RDMA_BYPASS_SHADOW | RDMA_READ_WORK_REG in DISP_REG_RDMA_SHADOW_UPDATE),
a 48992-byte RDMA0 FIFO (3062 16-byte entries) with zero video-mode
output valid threshold (0x8bf60000), and a clean RDMA0 soft-reset when
handing over from an active bootloader pipeline.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <324514544+sysretq0@users.noreply.github.com>
